ing","-\t * mode is enabled.","-\t *","-\t * Because L7 egress proxy packets are generated in the host-namespace","-\t * and generated packets MUST adjust their MTU for ESP encapsulation","-\t * an IP route MTU adjustment exists for L7 egress proxy packets.","-\t *","-\t * When the L7 egress proxy generates packets an 'ip rule' in the host","-\t * namespace routes these packets into table 2005 which has a route","-\t * toward 'cilium_host' and adjusts the MTU correctly for ESP encap.","-\t *","-\t * When 'cil_from_host@cilium_host' is reached the skb's mark is zeroed","-\t * and the packet is pushed toward 'cil_to_host@cilium_net'.","-\t *","-\t * If we simply let this packet drop to the stack, an iptables rule","-\t * exists which will mark the packet with 0x200 and trigger a local","-\t * delivery as part of L7 Proxy TPROXY mechanism.","-\t *","-\t * This iptables rule, created by","-\t * iptables.Manager.inboundProxyRedirectRule() is ignored by the mark","-\t * MARK_MAGIC_SKIP_TPROXY, in the control plane.","-\t * Technically, it is also ignored by MARK_MAGIC_ENCRYPT but reusing","-\t * this mark breaks further processing as its used in the XFRM subsystem.","-\t *","-\t * Therefore, if the packet's mark is zero, indicating it was forwarded","-\t * from 'cilium_host', mark the packet with MARK_MAGIC_SKIP_TPROXY","-\t * and allow it to enter the foward path once punted to stack.","-\t */","-\tif (ctx->mark == 0 && CONFIG(interface_ifindex) == CONFIG(cilium_net_ifindex))","-\t\tctx->mark = MARK_MAGIC_SKIP_TPROXY;","+\t\t/* Since v1.18 Cilium performs IPsec encryption at the native device,","+\t\t * before the packet leaves the host.","+\t\t *","+\t\t * A special case exists for L7 egress proxy packets when native routing","+\t\t * mode is enabled.","+\t\t *","+\t\t * Because L7 egress proxy packets are generated in the host-namespace","+\t\t * and generated packets MUST adjust their MTU for ESP encapsulation","+\t\t * an IP route MTU adjustment exists for L7 egress proxy packets.","+\t\t *","+\t\t * When the L7 egress proxy generates packets an 'ip rule' in the host","+\t\t * namespace routes these packets into table 2005 which has a route","+\t\t * toward 'cilium_host' and adjusts the MTU correctly for ESP encap.","+\t\t *","+\t\t * When 'cil_from_host@cilium_host' is reached the skb's mark is zeroed","+\t\t * and the packet is pushed toward 'cil_to_host@cilium_net'.","+\t\t *","+\t\t * If we simply let this packet drop to the stack, an iptables rule","+\t\t * exists which will mark the packet with 0x200 and trigger a local","+\t\t * delivery as part of L7 Proxy TPROXY mechanism.","+\t\t *","+\t\t * This iptables rule, created by","+\t\t * iptables.Manager.inboundProxyRedirectRule() is ignored by the mark","+\t\t * MARK_MAGIC_SKIP_TPROXY, in the control plane.","+\t\t * Technically, it is also ignored by MARK_MAGIC_ENCRYPT but reusing","+\t\t * this mark breaks further processing as its used in the XFRM subsystem.","+\t\t *","+\t\t * Therefore, if the packet's mark is zero, indicating it was forwarded","+\t\t * from 'cilium_host', mark the packet with MARK_MAGIC_SKIP_TPROXY","+\t\t * and allow it to enter the foward path once punted to stack.","+\t\t */","+\t\tif (ctx->mark == 0 && CONFIG(interface_ifindex) == CONFIG(cilium_net_ifindex))","+\t\t\tctx->mark = MARK_MAGIC_SKIP_TPROXY;"," #endif /* !TUNNEL_MODE */"," "," # ifdef ENABLE_NODEPORT","-\tif (ctx_is_encrypt(ctx) && validate_ethertype(ctx, &proto)) {","-\t\t/* handle_nat_fwd() tail calls in the majority of cases, so control","-\t\t * might never return to this program. Since IPsec is not compatible","-\t\t * iwth Host Firewall, this won't be an issue.","-\t\t */","-\t\tret = handle_nat_fwd(ctx, 0, src_id, proto, true, &trace, &ext_err);","-\t\tif (IS_ERR(ret))","-\t\t\tgoto out;","+\t\tif (ctx_is_encrypt(ctx) && validate_ethertype(ctx, &proto)) {","+\t\t\t/* handle_nat_fwd() tail calls in the majority of cases, so control","+\t\t\t * might never return to this program. 